 state; focused tracks terminal focus (via tea.FocusMsg/BlurMsg) so notifications are suppressed while the user is already looking. Focus reporting isn't supported by every terminal (see tea.BlurMsg docs), so focused defaults to false ("not known to be focused") — when in doubt, notify rather than silently suppress. set by applyEvent, consumed by the eventMsg handler P16.5 mouse selection & click-to-focus: sel is documented on the selection type; focusedIdx is the transcript segment index most recently single-clicked (-1 for none) and drives the left accent bar in renderTranscriptContent — purely a visual affordance, gates nothing. search (P40.3) is non-nil while the incremental transcript-search overlay is active: it captures keyboard input, greps the transcript's rendered content, and drives match navigation. See search.go. approvalState holds the details of a pending tool-execution approval request plus the option-list dialog state (TQ6). run id echoed back when answering highlighted dialog option suggested pattern for the "allow always" rule typing a deny reason the reason being typed todoStripItem is one entry in the live plan strip (TQ7). "pending" | "in_progress" | "done" clipboardResultMsg carries the result of an async clipboard write. pasteImageResultMsg carries the result of reading an image off the OS clipboard (P16.8). ok is false with a nil err when the clipboard simply held no image. pasteClipboardImageCmd returns a tea.Cmd that reads an image from the OS clipboard into a temp file. ollamaWarmedMsg reports the outcome of an async pre-warm attempt (P33.10). It carries no UI state — the warm-up is a latency optimization the user never sees directly — so the Update handler ignores it; the type exists only because a tea.Cmd must return a tea.Msg. maybeWarmOllamaCmd returns a tea.Cmd that pre-warms the Ollama model when it makes sense to (P33.10 lever 2), or nil when it doesn't. It is a no-op — returns nil — unless the provider is Ollama (OllamaBaseURL set